        content:
          '// qsm-langdev profile: general. Seeded by `qsm-langdev init`; the repo owns this\n// file. Without it knip has no entry point and reports every file as unused,\n// which is findings nobody can act on. Name what the outside calls: each\n// plugin\'s scripts, its hooks, and the gates. Whatever a named entry cannot\n// reach is dead code, which is the finding worth having.\n{\n  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@5/schema.json",\n  // A hooks module is register.tsx (JSX for its dialogs); a test file is an\n  // entry too, so a helper exported for its own test is used, not dead.\n  "entry": [\n    "plugins/*/scripts/*.ts",\n    "plugins/*/hooks/*.ts",\n    "plugins/*/hooks/*.tsx",\n    ".gates/*.ts",\n    "**/*.test.ts"\n  ],\n  "project": ["lib/**/*.ts", "plugins/**/*.ts", ".gates/**/*.ts"],\n  // Binaries a plugin\'s own installer puts on PATH rather than package\n  // dependencies: knip cannot see where they come from and would report\n  // each as unlisted.\n  "ignoreBinaries": ["sentrux"]\n}\n',
